cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "art-provenance-check"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Majores
abstract: >-
  Open-source provenance due diligence for the art trade. The tool parses
  catalogue provenance texts in German and English, maps the years 1933 to
  1945 as documented, inferred or open, flags ownership changes, seizure and
  restitution keywords, and matches names against a reference list built from
  Wikidata (Art Looting Investigation Unit, Nazi-era looted art, restitution
  cases). It writes PDF audit records following the German Cultural Property
  Protection Act (KGSG, sections 42 to 45), reviews whole auction catalogues
  from CSV, and classifies print processes (offset reproduction, inkjet or
  giclee, stone lithography) from macro photos via Fourier spectrum analysis.
  It runs locally with a web interface. Results are research hints, not legal
  advice.
keywords:
  - provenance research
  - art market
  - due diligence
  - Nazi-looted art
  - restitution
  - cultural property
  - KGSG
  - Wikidata
  - digital humanities
  - print authentication
  - Fourier analysis
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Thesimpleex/art-provenance-check"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
